1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,683
Why does cutting an onion make you cry?

2
00:00:02,983 --> 00:00:04,706
A whole onion doesn't.

3
00:00:04,706 --> 00:00:05,881
Only a cut one.

4
00:00:06,381 --> 00:00:13,110
Inside each cell, the onion keeps two things apart: a harmless sulfur compound, and an enzyme.

5
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:16,103
Your knife breaks the cells, and the two mix.

6
00:00:16,703 --> 00:00:20,281
A second enzyme turns the result into a stinging gas.

7
00:00:20,781 --> 00:00:24,528
It drifts up and reaches the nerves on the surface of your eye.

8
00:00:24,828 --> 00:00:29,510
Your eye does the only thing it can: it makes tears to wash it away.

9
00:00:30,010 --> 00:00:33,877
Chill the onion first, and the enzymes work more slowly.

10
00:00:34,177 --> 00:00:39,334
Scientists have even made onions with almost none of that second enzyme.

11
00:00:39,334 --> 00:00:41,125
They hardly make you cry.

12
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:42,945
The onion isn't sad.

13
00:00:42,945 --> 00:00:46,114
It's a chemical trap, and your knife springs it.
